Follow the gpu-screen-recorder process the service starts instead of finding
it by name every 2 seconds.

Upstream goes idle as soon as it sends the stop signal. A process check that
lands while the recorder is still saving adopts it as an externally started
recording, and when it exits the "Recording saved" notification is shown a
second time. The recorder is now launched through runStream with a wrapper
that prints its pid and, once it has exited, its exit status. The service
signals only that pid and settles the capture only on its exit. setsid keeps
the recorder out of the stream's process group, which Noctalia kills when it
ends a stream on reload or exit.

The Flatpak branch is untested: signals go to the flatpak process, not the
recorder inside it. Related upstream issue:
https://github.com/noctalia-dev/official-plugins/issues/84

